# LLVM coverage output from the Xcode-instrumented HadesApp binary, written to its process CWD
# on exit (seen at the repo root and at Mac/HadesApp). Regenerated every run, never committed.
# Bare filenames match at any depth, so this covers both locations.
default.profraw

# Keep memory tracked
!.arcforge/memory/

# .mcp.json is deliberately NOT ignored, and must not be. A bare `.mcp.json` pattern matches at
# ANY depth, which silently excluded ClaudeCodePlugin/.mcp.json - the v2 Claude Code plugin's own
# manifest. scripts/sync-plugin.sh aborts without it ("missing its manifest or .mcp.json") and
# release.yml validates it, so the plugin publish fails on any fresh checkout while working fine
# on the machine that has the file untracked. It carries no machine-specific state: a static HTTP
# entry pointing at 127.0.0.1:7823.

# Superpowers artifacts
docs/

# No .meta files belong in this repository. It is not a Unity project and is not consumed as a
# Unity package; the Unity plugin ships source only, and Unity generates .meta in the USER's
# project on import (PluginInstaller writes none - see its doc comment). Ignoring them outright
# means opening this checkout in Unity, or dropping it inside a Unity project, cannot quietly add
# a single one.
*.meta
